The upstream Color Scheme - Default and Theme - Default packages do not
include an open-source license notice. LicenseRef-Upstream-Unspecified
records that fact; this notice does not grant or imply an upstream license.
The MIT license of the separate sublimehq/Packages repository is not asserted
to cover these bundled resources.

The light variant retains the previous custom Spyder adaptation by Andres
Montoya and the Spyder Team. It is not an official Sublime Text light scheme.
The earlier theme metadata declared that adaptation MIT; this notice does not
relicense those existing contributions or assert a new license for them.

This directory contains Spyder-specific YAML palette and semantic mappings.
It does not bundle original Sublime Text theme files, application code,
icons, textures, or fonts. Bracket fills, variable explorer groups, and
Help/Appeal/Pydoc colors are adaptations for Qt/Spyder.
